      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Problem: multi-precision deployment still behaves like multi-model deployment"
        }
      ]
    },
    "shape-1": {
      "left": 0.25,
      "top": 1.5,
      "width": 12.83,
      "height": 0.5,
      "overlap": {
        "overlapping_shapes": {
          "shape-0": 4.8
        }
      },
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Matryoshka Quantization targets the maintenance and quality gap created when each bit-width is optimized separately.",
          "font_size": 11.0,
          "bold": true,
          "italic": false,
          "color": "000000"
        }
      ]
    },
    "shape-2": {
      "left": 1.1,
      "top": 3.03,
      "width": 9.6,
      "height": 5.07,
      "placeholder_type": "BODY",
      "default_font_size": 36.0,
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "1. Deployment pressure",
          "font_name": "Aptos",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": "LLM decoding is often memory-bandwidth limited, so weight movement from HBM/SRAM becomes a major inference cost.",
          "level": 1,
          "font_name": "Aptos"
        },
        {
          "text": "Weight quantization reduces communication cost and makes int8, int4, and int2 attractive serving formats.",
          "level": 1,
          "font_name": "Aptos"
        }
      ]
    },
    "shape-3": {
      "left": 12.22,
      "top": 8.34,
      "width": 3.6,
      "height": 0.48,
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "1",
          "font_size": 12.0,
          "color": "595959"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "slide-1": {
    "shape-0": {
      "left": 1.1,
      "top": 0.48,
      "width": 9.6,
      "height": 1.74,
      "placeholder_type": "TITLE",
      "default_font_size": 54.0,
      "overlap": {
        "overlapping_shapes": {
          "shape-1": 4.8
        }
      },
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Core idea: train one parent integer model whose MSBs are useful slices"
        }
      ]
    },
    "shape-1": {
      "left": 0.25,
      "top": 1.5,
      "width": 12.83,
      "height": 0.5,
      "overlap": {
        "overlapping_shapes": {
          "shape-0": 4.8
        }
      },
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "MatQuant uses the natural nested structure of integer bit planes: lower precision models are extracted from the most significant bits of the same quantized weights.",
          "font_size": 11.0,
          "bold": true,
          "italic": false,
          "color": "000000"
        }
      ]
    },
    "shape-2": {
      "left": 1.1,
      "top": 3.03,
      "width": 9.6,
      "height": 5.07,
      "placeholder_type": "BODY",
      "default_font_size": 36.0,
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "1. Nest",
          "font_name": "Aptos",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Start from a higher-precision integer representation, e.g. int8.",
          "level": 1,
          "font_name": "Aptos"
        },
        {
          "text": "Slice the most significant bits to obtain int4 or int2 without storing a separate model.",
          "level": 1,
          "font_name": "Aptos"
        }
      ]
    },
    "shape-3": {
      "left": 12.22,
      "top": 8.34,
      "width": 3.6,
      "height": 0.48,
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "2",
          "font_size": 12.0,
          "color": "595959"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "slide-2": {
    "shape-0": {
      "left": 1.1,
      "top": 0.48,
      "width": 9.6,
      "height": 1.74,
      "placeholder_type": "TITLE",
      "default_font_size": 54.0,
      "overlap": {
        "overlapping_shapes": {
          "shape-1": 4.8
        }
      },
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Observation: co-training changes how quantization buckets are used"
        }
      ]
    },
    "shape-1": {
      "left": 0.25,
      "top": 1.5,
      "width": 12.83,
      "height": 0.5,
      "overlap": {
        "overlapping_shapes": {
          "shape-0": 4.8
        }
      },
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "The paper's main empirical observation is that MatQuant is not just truncating int8; training reshapes the quantized weight distribution.",
          "font_size": 11.0,
          "bold": true,
          "italic": false,
          "color": "000000"
        }
      ]
    },
    "shape-2": {
      "left": 1.1,
      "top": 3.03,
      "width": 9.6,
      "height": 5.07,
      "placeholder_type": "BODY",
      "default_font_size": 36.0,
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "1. Right-shifted buckets",
          "font_name": "Aptos",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": "MatQuant shifts quantized weights toward higher-valued buckets.",
          "level": 1,
          "font_name": "Aptos"
        },
        {
          "text": "int8 and int4 have enough buckets that small shifts do not strongly hurt quality.",
          "level": 1,
          "font_name": "Aptos"
        }
      ]
    },
    "shape-3": {
      "left": 12.22,
      "top": 8.34,
      "width": 3.6,
      "height": 0.48,
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "3",
          "font_size": 12.0,
          "color": "595959"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "slide-3": {
    "shape-0": {
      "left": 1.1,
      "top": 0.48,
      "width": 9.6,
      "height": 1.74,
      "placeholder_type": "TITLE",
      "default_font_size": 54.0,
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Results and takeaway: one checkpoint covers a denser accuracy-cost curve"
        }
      ]
    },
    "shape-1": {
      "left": 1.1,
      "top": 3.03,
      "width": 9.6,
      "height": 5.07,
      "placeholder_type": "BODY",
      "default_font_size": 36.0,
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "MatQuant keeps high-bit quality near independently trained baselines while improving the lowest-bit slice, which is the hard case.",
          "font_name": "Aptos",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Bottom line: MatQuant reframes multi-precision quantization from \"train and serve many models\" to \"train one nested parent model and slice it at deployment time.\"",
          "level": 1,
          "font_name": "Aptos"
        }
      ]
    },
    "shape-2": {
